questions.prompt:
What does this code log?
```js
try {
  console.log("A");
  JSON.parse("{ bad json }");
  console.log("B");
} catch (error) {
  console.log("C");
}
```

What does this code log?
```js
try {
  console.log("A");
  throw new Error("Failed");
} catch (error) {
  console.log("B");
} finally {
  console.log("C");
}
```

What does this function return?
```js
function example() {
  try {
    return "try";
  } finally {
    return "finally";
  }
}

example();
```

What does this code log?
```js
function test() {
  throw new Error("Failed");
  return "Done";
}

try {
  console.log(test());
} catch (error) {
  console.log(error.message);
}
```

What kind of error is this most likely to produce?
```js
const user = undefined;
console.log(user.name);
```

What is the problem with this catch block?
```js
try {
  riskyOperation();
} catch (error) {
  // do nothing
}
```

What does this code log?
```js
class ValidationError extends Error {}

const error = new ValidationError("Invalid");

console.log(error instanceof Error);
console.log(error instanceof ValidationError);
```

What should this code usually do for unexpected error types?
```js
try {
  createUser(data);
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof ValidationError) {
    showFormError(error.message);
  } else {
    // what here?
  }
}
```

Does this catch the thrown timer error?
```js
try {
  setTimeout(() => {
    throw new Error("Timer failed");
  }, 1000);
} catch (error) {
  console.log("Caught");
}
```
